WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.389 --> 00:00:02.972
(bright music)

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.140
- [Narrator] If you were alone in a room

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.483
with someone addicted to hard
drugs, what would you ask?

00:00:10.483 --> 00:00:12.900
(soft music)

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.340
- I'm Chad, nice to meet you.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.173
- Right on.

00:00:18.173 --> 00:00:19.736
I'm a Riggy Marz.

00:00:19.736 --> 00:00:21.811
♪ You ever been dope sick in the street ♪

00:00:21.811 --> 00:00:22.980
♪ Yeah, you know the vibe ♪

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.670
- What drug or drugs are you addicted to?

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.820
- Opiates, but whatever you got.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.320
- Did you start off with
something small, like marijuana?

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.550
- It started for me just like
already feeling really nervous

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.840
and like I don't fit in

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.910
mixed with a little bit of peer pressure.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.580
Come on, man. It'll relax you.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.480
Hit this.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.090
And my curiosity, I picked it up.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.980
- And you started off in high school?

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.660
- Eighth grade I would say.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.100
My sophomore year is when my
parents first put me in rehab.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.087
- Oh.

00:00:57.087 --> 00:00:57.920
- So I was 15.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.920
- How old are you?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.880
- I'm 35.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.380
- How long have you been using?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.990
- About 20 years.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.130
- What other drugs were-

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.060
- [Riggy Marz] Everything.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:06.990
- Everything?

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.990
- Ecstasy, ketamine, GHB,
psychedelics, powdered cocaine,

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:17.660
crack cocaine, meth, heroin,
and up until recently fentanyl.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.600
- So I was wondering if you
could just kind of walk me

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.440
through the first time
that you took drugs.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.740
- The first time I actually
got high off something

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.780
was inhalants.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.870
I was huffing WD40 out of a paper bag.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.090
I wanna say I was 12.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:38.190
I saw Leonardo de Caprio do it

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.900
in the movie, Basketball Diaries,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.400
and I was like, that looks cool.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.530
I'm gonna try that when
I get home from school.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.720
- What are some things
that are currently in place

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.970
in our society that are
enabling your addiction

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.370
or hindering your recovery?

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.410
- Criminalizing us.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.800
Just taking advantage of
a mentally ill person.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.430
And then you have that
title over you forever.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.250
I've tried to apply for jobs recently

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:06.930
and they run my background
and they won't hire me

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:11.280
because of some (beep) that I
did seven or eight years ago.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.140
So that's kind of enabling

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.520
because it's like, all right, (beep) it,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.540
I'm just gonna use.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.860
- I am a police sergeant

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.080
with the local law enforcement agency.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.410
What were your thoughts
when you were arrested?

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.620
- My thoughts were, I
shouldn't be getting arrested

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.453
for this.

00:02:26.453 --> 00:02:28.560
That happening repeatedly,

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.530
now I'm just like in and out
of county jail, in and out.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.870
And all I wanted to do was just get high

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.460
because I don't like how I feel.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.990
I don't like myself.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.823
- Right.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:41.250
So is that one of the reasons
why you did do heroin?

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.270
You didn't like yourself?

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.580
- Yeah. I've been doing it so long

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.700
I couldn't think of another solution.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.230
- So because of those experiences

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.680
did you have a negative
view of people like me?

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:53.550
- Oh yeah.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.383
- Okay.

00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:55.354
- Yeah.

00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:56.760
Like you guys were the enemy,

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.760
but I've met a few really
cool police officers though

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.400
that have talked to me,
not at me or down on me.

00:03:08.142 --> 00:03:12.259
Talked to me face to
face like a human being.

00:03:12.259 --> 00:03:17.259
Yeah, I grew to not like cops very much.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.590
- Okay. That's fine.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.597
And I understand that

00:03:20.597 --> 00:03:25.290
because your experiences
weren't all always great.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.750
But just to let you know,
we're not all like that.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.680
So what could we do
better for drug addicts?

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.300
- I can't say don't arrest them

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.255
if they get caught with something,

00:03:35.255 --> 00:03:37.650
obviously you have to or whatever,

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.050
but maybe give them a little pep talk

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.141
on the drive to downtown.

00:03:42.141 --> 00:03:45.720
Like it's nothing personal

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.760
but you should get some help, man.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.200
- I'm the marketing director

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.630
for an addiction treatment
and trauma center.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.280
You said you're a chronic relapser.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.160
So it sounds like you've
tried to get clean sometimes.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.590
Can you tell me about those experiences?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:03.590
- Yeah, I would go to AA meetings

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.703
but just the meetings.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.030
So I was dry.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:12.120
Eventually you get to
a point where your body

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:16.743
and your brain is just like
screaming at you to use.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:23.640
It comes down to your higher power,

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.040
it comes down to...

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.742
We use drugs to fill this God-sized hole

00:04:30.742 --> 00:04:34.170
that only God or spirituality

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.030
or that a higher power can fill.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.250
So I pray and meditate and stuff.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.780
I'm not religious by any means,

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:44.250
but that's when I'm having
a rough day or month,

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:48.347
that's usually what keeps me going smooth.

00:04:48.347 --> 00:04:50.760
- When you think about treatment

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.980
or you think about the
process of getting clean,

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.930
what feelings come up for you?

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.243
- Just utter hopelessness.

00:05:03.351 --> 00:05:08.268
And when people look at recovery
or the destination, right?

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:13.140
The mountain is so (beep) big,

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.920
it just seems impossible
to ever get there.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.990
- What do you think is
the best and worst advice

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.540
that you've heard regarding addiction?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:26.280
- The worst advice I've
heard has gotta be relapse

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:31.260
is part of the process,
because it doesn't have to be.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:36.003
And I know people that were
clean that used that excuse,

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:41.223
relapse it's part of the
process, and never came back.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:44.553
They're dead.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.423
I've used that excuse before.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:54.030
- Hi, I'm Jessica and I'm an alcoholic.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:55.620
I'm three years sober.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:56.670
- That is amazing.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.950
- Was there anything in
particular that happened

00:05:58.950 --> 00:05:59.783
that made you use...

00:05:59.783 --> 00:06:01.260
Are you using to-

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.670
- [Riggy Marz] I was born with the gene.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:03.570
- You were born with the gene.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:04.650
- [Riggy Marz] Yeah.
- Okay.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:05.483
And from the-

00:06:05.483 --> 00:06:06.510
- I'm dual diagnosed.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:10.230
So I can have the addiction
part under control,

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.810
but I have mental health issues too.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.560
So if I don't have that in
check, I'm gonna get loaded.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.810
- I was also dual diagnosed with anxiety,

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.850
depression and alcoholism.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.220
So do you have a therapist now?

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:24.053
- I do.

00:06:24.053 --> 00:06:24.886
- Okay, cool.

00:06:24.886 --> 00:06:27.480
- Yeah, I need all that outside help too.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.360
At one point I was against suboxone.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.358
- [Jessica] Yeah.

00:06:31.358 --> 00:06:32.910
- And methadone, saying that's not sober

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.310
but whatever keeps you from dying.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.143
- [Jessica] Yeah.

00:06:36.143 --> 00:06:40.046
- Recovery's not so black and white,

00:06:40.046 --> 00:06:45.046
a lot of old timers in
AA make it up to be.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:50.130
When I learned that, it
gave me a lot less anxiety

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:53.340
thinking about my own
situation and my own path.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.840
- So my mom is an addict

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:58.920
and also alcoholism has
ran through my family.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.660
Since I've grown up they've been like,

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.130
oh, you have the alcoholic gene,

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.180
you have the addictive gene.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.520
So you need to be extra careful

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.080
especially when you go in college.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.070
And with my mom, I've had to
go between that back and forth

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.830
of just like that just hope.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.740
It's like, oh, you're doing really good.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.740
And I'm so proud of you and I love you.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:23.190
And then it's just like, she relapses

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:26.670
and it just starts all over again.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:31.670
And it's like every time it
just makes me resent her more

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.390
because as a kid, it's
like my love wasn't enough.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.360
And it broke me down so much

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.580
because it was like I was
just getting so hopeful

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.960
and then it would just be that
cycle of just being scared,

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.000
like, oh, where is she?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.233
Is she alive?

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:52.830
Am I gonna see her again?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.963
I wish I said, I loved her.

00:07:57.352 --> 00:08:02.352
- I have a son and oh man it
would kill me if he hated me

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:04.613
because of that.

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.620
I told him, "Hey, you know all those times

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:14.100
that grandma told you that I was on tour?"

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.153
and he's like, "Yeah.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.690
I told him I was in jail.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.190
I was in jail and I'm an addict

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:26.970
and I'm a sick person, but
right now I'm not so sick,

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:28.410
I'm getting better.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:32.703
But with my son, I don't
leave anything out.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:38.353
Because I don't want him
to go seek elder advice

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.270
from another kid in the neighborhood.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:43.980
I want him to come to me.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:45.030
You know what I mean?

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.150
So I can keep it real with him.

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.013
And the trust is there.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.460
- What is your biggest fear in life?

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.653
- That is a really hard question.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:02.840
My biggest fear in life
is ending up alone.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:06.543
Being old and living in regret.

00:09:07.899 --> 00:09:11.280
- [Interviewer] Is that also
how you found comfort in drugs?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.427
- Yeah. I didn't care
about any of that (beep).

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:18.533
- It was just like it was something

00:09:18.533 --> 00:09:20.460
that was always kind of there for you.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:21.293
- Yeah.

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:22.471
- [Interviewer] When no one else was.

00:09:22.471 --> 00:09:25.410
- Yeah, yeah exactly.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.243
- Yeah.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.126
It was so nice meeting you.

00:09:29.126 --> 00:09:30.561
- Pleasure.

00:09:30.561 --> 00:09:31.662
- I'm so proud of you.

00:09:31.662 --> 00:09:33.458
- Thank you.
- Of what you've accomplished

00:09:33.458 --> 00:09:34.905
and just where you have to go.

00:09:34.905 --> 00:09:35.775
- Thank you.

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:36.816
- Nice to meet you, man.
- Nice to meet you.

00:09:36.816 --> 00:09:37.649
- What's up man?

00:09:37.649 --> 00:09:38.566
- What's up.
- How're you doing?

00:09:38.566 --> 00:09:39.399
- Nice to meet you.

00:09:39.399 --> 00:09:40.232
- Nice to meet you.

00:09:40.232 --> 00:09:41.133
- Thank you so much.

00:09:41.133 --> 00:09:42.148
- Yes, can I hug you?

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:44.354
Okay. Nice to meet you.

00:09:44.354 --> 00:09:45.187
- Nice to meet you too.

00:09:45.187 --> 00:09:46.517
Congrats on your three years.

00:09:46.517 --> 00:09:47.447
- Thank you.

00:09:47.447 --> 00:09:48.280
Thank you.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.850
I hope that one day you'll also say

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:52.140
you have three years too.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.190
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

